{
  "$comment": [
    "CAPTURE RECORDS for cinatra#2841 (PR #2866), in the shape",
    "scripts/ci/lib/capture-record-contract.mjs validates.",
    "",
    "RE-SHOT IN FULL after eye-grading found a fourth conformance defect: every chip printed the",
    "skill's SLUG (blog-post-matcher) where section V draws a natural-language name and the owning",
    "extension's manifest declares one (cinatra.displayName). The label is now resolved once,",
    "server-side, onto RankedRecommendation.displayName and read by every place the card prints a",
    "skill. These nine records REPLACE the nine registered by the previous round (delete-first, same",
    "recorder id and contract); the pictures they cite were taken by one run of the recorder against",
    "the fixed build, and the settled cells were driven from a parked, undecided run by pressing the",
    "chips' own controls in that same run.",
    "",
    "THESE RECORDS ARE REGISTERED in scripts/ci/chat-hitl-capture-index.json, which the previous",
    "round could not do. That round's records carried the count 0 they truthfully observed for",
    "[data-lifecycle-card=\"recommendation_hold\"] and [data-lifecycle-card-host=\"run_card\"], because",
    "the shipped row emitted neither attribute -- so no honest recommendation_hold record could",
    "satisfy its own contract. Finding 3 of commit 1d95dd06a closed that: the row IS the card, so the",
    "row's outermost element now declares kind, host and held/decided exactly as ReviewGateCard does.",
    "Every record below observed all three on the screen it was taken on, and the counts here are the",
    "ones the recorder actually measured -- an anchor it did not look for is absent, not zero-filled.",
    "",
    "COUNTING SCOPES (from the recorder, restated so every number is re-derivable):",
    "  frame -- document.querySelectorAll(sel).length on the document the picture was taken in;",
    "  root  -- the card root's own subtree INCLUDING the root element."
  ],
